 "region": "Ming China",
 "_about": "a baochuan of Zheng He's fleets (1405-1433): a great flat-bottomed junk with a broad transom bow and a towering stern of two storeys of cabins, the rudder hung deep in its well, six masts with battened red-brown sails -- the foremost raked over the bow, the after ones stepped off the centre line -- painted eyes at the bow, a gallery round the stern. (Sized as the 2000-liao ships the Longjiang shipyard's rudderposts suggest and the Nanjing reconstruction follows, about 60 m by 14 m; the chronicles' 125 m is doubted)",
